# Turntable UI

Photoreal deck. Change light/materials with the existing token model — do not stack extra blend layers.

## Machine

- Walnut frame, screws **centered in the wood rail** (`padding: 1.7rem`, screws `0.85rem` from edges — not in the vertex)
- Wide plinth: square platter left, console right (title, time, cue slider, VU, keys)
- Size: keep the machine large enough that titles wrap little. Console column must stay wide (`aspect-ratio` ~1.62, platter capped so readout has room)
- Tonearm: gimbal / cue / anti-skate **fixed on the deck**. Tube + counterweight + headshell rotate around pivot `418, 78` (`.tonearm-swing`, `transform-origin: 418px 78px`). Real pivoted arm (Technics/Dual) — do not rotate the gimbal

## Vinyl

- Picture disc: thumbnail printed on the playing surface (dark, desaturated), **grooves overlay**, paper label stays in the center
- Grooves: wide, low-contrast, slight blur. **Never** a second sub-pixel `repeating-radial-gradient` sparkle — that causes moiré / “squiggly” rings
- Specular is **world-fixed** (siblings of `.vinyl-spin`, not inside it): circular catch at `--ref-x` / `--ref-y`. No radar-rotate, no rectangular “window pane”

## Lighting

One circular key light orbiting the room (~72s ellipse from upper-left). JS on `.stage` sets `--light-x/y`, `--ref-x/y`, `--light-az`, `--shadow-x/y`.
- Room wash: `circle … vmin`, not `ellipse W% H%` (ellipses look like pancakes on wide screens)
- Shadow opposite the light, plus a downward contact shadow
- `prefers-reduced-motion`: skip the orbit; do not spin the disc
- Do not add competing shafts, `machine::after` sheens, or a strong album-color wash

## Hardware extras

- VU: shared pivot `(50, 58)`, arc r=36, needle 34, sweep ±48°. Keep SVG unstretched
- Cue slider: milled metal fader under the timer (`.cue-rail`), not a generic 1px web range
- Keys match existing `.deck-key` chrome. New controls must look machined into the plinth
- Playlist picker is a **record-shop bin** (`.bin` / `.pressing`). Click a jacket to select that playlist and open the **liner**; click the same jacket again to close. **Acquire** is a sealed empty jacket; opening it uses the same liner with a paste-URL form, not a modal. One horizontal row: centered when they fit; **8+ pressings switch to spines** (`data-spines`) — hover/focus pulls a jacket out. Edge-fade + snap-scroll when they overflow.

## Motion

One room, one settle. Do not mix default Motion easings, Tailwind `transition-*`, or unmatched durations.

- Curve: `--ease` / `easeRoom` = `cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1)`
- Room objects (jackets, liner, title, cover, spines): `--motion` = **380ms**. Liner presence via CSS `data-open`. Identity swaps via `fade` / `fadeLift` in `lib/motion.ts`. Click outside closes the sleeve via a **transparent** dismiss layer — the room stays lit. Also Close, Esc, or the same jacket.
- Chrome (keys, `.hw-btn`, field focus): `--motion-chrome` = **240ms**, plus a 1px press on `:active`
- Tonearm only: `--motion-arm` = **700ms**. Vinyl spin and VU stay mechanical — do not CSS-ease them
- `prefers-reduced-motion`: no spin, no transitions
